meta {
  name: Cancel Row Policy
  type: http
  seq: 74
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/assigned/{{reconAssignRowId}}/cancel-policy
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "other",
    "note": "Non-payment",
    "cancelledOn": "2026-10-20"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("the outcome is done, linking the chargeback", function () {
    const outcome = res.getBody().row.outcome;
    expect(outcome.kind).to.equal("chargeback");
    expect(outcome.status).to.equal("done");
    expect(outcome.step).to.equal(null);
    expect(outcome.policyId).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconChargebackPolicyId"));
    expect(outcome.chargebackId).to.be.a("string");
    expect(outcome.completedBy.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("currentUserId"));
  });

  test("and the row is decided as a chargeback, by the assignee", function () {
    const review = res.getBody().row.review;
    expect(review.status).to.equal("resolved");
    expect(review.resolution).to.equal("chargeback_recorded");
    expect(review.note).to.equal("The carrier cancelled it in October");
  });

  test("the policy is off the books, on the carrier's date", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.policy.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconChargebackPolicyId"));
    expect(body.policy.active).to.equal(false);
    expect(body.policy.policyStatus).to.equal("Cancelled");
    expect(body.policy.cancellation.reason).to.equal("other");
    expect(body.policy.cancellation.note).to.equal("Non-payment");
    expect(body.policy.cancellation.cancelledOn).to.equal("2026-10-20");
    expect(body.policy.cancellation.chargebackId).to.equal(body.row.outcome.chargebackId);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /carrier-reconciliation/assigned/:rowId/cancel-policy

  A **Chargeback** outcome's second step (PAC-173 PR 6): cancel the policy its
  sale booked, **with the chargeback**, dated on the carrier's cancellation
  date — and finish the row. The household page's Cancel dialog, ticked and
  locked, posts here.

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation` (enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:read` **or** `leads:read` (the
    assignee's class gate), and — as for the sale before it —
    `leads:write` **and** `deal_audits:write`, checked in the service
  - **Data scope:** the row's assignee only; the owner records on no row

  Why a row endpoint and not `Cancel Household Policy` carrying the row id
  (as the Sold form does): the policies and clients modules sit under the
  reconciliation module, so they cannot call back into it. Here the cancel,
  the ledger row and the outcome commit **in one transaction**.

  ## Body
  | Field | Type | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `reason` | `"sold" \| "changed_carrier" \| "other"` | required, the Cancel button's vocabulary |
  | `note` | string ≤ 500, nullable | **required for `other`**; dropped for the named reasons |
  | `cancelledOn` | `YYYY-MM-DD` | **required** — the carrier's cancellation date. Not in the future, not before the sale (agency calendar) |

  ## What it does
  - Cancels the policy as `Cancel Household Policy` does (status, `active`,
    household recount, edit log "Policy cancelled, chargeback recorded").
  - Writes a `chargebacks` row: `reason: "cancellation"`, `amount` = the
    policy's premium, charged to the producer credited on the deal, dated
    `cancelledOn`. **Inside a calendar month of the sale** the deal's
    `chargebackAdjustment` moves by `-premium` (the producer's sold credit is
    reversed); after it, only the chargeback stands.
  - Finishes the outcome (`chargebackId` linked) and resolves the row
    `chargeback_recorded`, by the assignee.

  **It cancels only a policy numbered as the Dash line.** The sale links the
  deal's policy whose number keys as Dash's; with none, it links the deal's
  only policy, and with several it links none — never a guess, since this
  charges money back. Correcting the number on the sale and retrying (or
  Continue) links it.

  A row already finished as a chargeback answers `201` unchanged. A policy
  already cancelled **with** a cancellation chargeback (from the household
  page) finishes the row with that one.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  { "row": { …the row as GET assigned/:rowId answers it, outcome done… },
    "policy": { "id": "…", "policyStatus": "Cancelled", "active": false, …,
      "cancellation": { "reason": "other", "note": "Non-payment",
        "cancelledAt": "2026-10-30T15:04:05.000Z", "cancelledOn": "2026-10-20",
        "chargebackId": "…" } } }
  ```

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | Validation; a `cancelledOn` in the future or before the sale; `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_NOT_ALLOWED` — the row is not being recorded as a chargeback |
  | 403 | `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_FORBIDDEN` — without `leads:write` + `deal_audits:write` |
  | 404 | No such row in the agency, or not the caller's |
  | 409 | The sale is not booked yet; `RECONCILIATION_CHARGEBACK_POLICY_UNMATCHED` — none of the sale's policies is numbered as the Dash line (correct the number on the sale, then retry or Continue); the policy is already off the books without a chargeback (the owner decides the row by hand); the row was decided; its run was replaced or did not finish; a concurrent change |
}
